=== 1. Sign of w0 + wa + 1 on the corridor ===
w0 + wa + 1 = -(w_0 + 1)/2
solve(w0 + wa + 1 < 0) over reals: Interval.open(-1, oo)
at w0 = -1 (LambdaCDM point): 0
general slope k: w0 + wa + 1 = -(k - 1)*(w_0 + 1)  -> negative for t = 1 + w0 > 0 iff k > 1
  with t = 1 + w0: -t*(k - 1)

=== 2. Where the corridor's CPL line crosses -1 ===
a_c (any CPL line) = (w_0 + w_a + 1)/w_a
on wa = -k(1+w0):  a_c = (k - 1)/k ,  z_c = 1/(k - 1)   (independent of w0)
corridor k = 3/2:  a_c = 1/3 ,  z_c = 2
literature-style k = 1.58 (dagger, model memory, for comparison only): z_c = 1.724
k = 1 (boundary): oo  ; k = 3: 1/2

=== 3. Slope needed for a CPL crossing at DR2's quoted z ~ 0.4 ===
k such that z_c = 0.4: [7/2]  -> wa = -7/2 (1 + w0)
ratio to the corridor's 1.5: 7/3 = 2.333
w0 + wa + 1 for k = 7/2: -5*(w_0 + 1)/2

=== 4. The corridor's CPL w(z) + 1, as a multiple of (1 + w0) ===
(w(z) + 1)/(1 + w0) = -(z - 2)/(2*(z + 1))
   z = 0       (w+1)/(1+w0) = +1.0000
   z = 2/5     (w+1)/(1+w0) = +0.5714
   z = 1       (w+1)/(1+w0) = +0.2500
   z = 3/2     (w+1)/(1+w0) = +0.1000
   z = 2       (w+1)/(1+w0) = +0.0000
   z = 233/100 (w+1)/(1+w0) = -0.0495
   z = 5       (w+1)/(1+w0) = -0.2500
   z = 1090    (w+1)/(1+w0) = -0.4986
   z -> oo  (w+1)/(1+w0) = -1/2
zero of (w+1) at z = [2] ; (w+1) > 0 on 0 <= z < 2, so the corridor's CPL line is not phantom on 0.4 < z < 2

