=== 5. Taylor reading: k = d ln(1 + w)/d ln a at a = 1 ===
k (Taylor CPL) = Subs(Derivative(f(a), a), a, 1)/f(1)  ; d ln(1+w)/d ln a |_(a=1) = Subs(Derivative(f(a), a), a, 1)/f(1)  ; equal: True
So a never-phantom field lands in the CPL crossing quadrant (Taylor reading) iff its 1 + w
grows faster than a^1 today; 1 + w ~ a^p gives k = p. Thawing from rest in matter domination
has 1 + w ~ a^3 at early times (field speed ~ t, kinetic energy ~ t^2 ~ a^3).
example 1 + w = eps a^p: k = p
matter era, constant slope: phi_dot = c t with c = -Vprime/3 ; kinetic energy ~ t^2; a ~ t^(2/3) => KE ~ a^3
